<https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002164> a skos:Concept;
  dc:identifier "homoit0002164";
  dc:issued "2022-07-04"^^xsd:date;
  dc:modified "2024-07-31"^^xsd:date;
  rdfs:comment "Japanese word that literally translates to \"rotten girl\" and is used to describe young women who enjoy media or fanworks focused on romantic or sexual relationships between men. Some fans self-identify as fujoshis, typically as a form of playful self-deprecation, but it can also be considered derogatory."@en;
  skos:broader <https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002218>;
  skos:hasTopConcept <https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001345>;
  skos:inScheme <https://homosaurus.org/v3>;
  skos:prefLabel "Fujoshi"@ja .

<https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002206> a skos:Concept;
  dc:identifier "homoit0002206";
  dc:issued "2022-07-04"^^xsd:date;
  dc:modified "2022-12-16"^^xsd:date;
  rdfs:comment "Fan-created photo manipulations or deepfakes depicting sexual or romantic relationships between characters from various media properties. Typically erotic or pornographic in nature. Historically used for male-male couples only, but is now used more broadly; includes femslash manips."@en;
  skos:broader <https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002204>;
  skos:hasTopConcept <https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001345>;
  skos:inScheme <https://homosaurus.org/v3>;
  skos:prefLabel "Slash manips"@en .

